# Elesh Norn, Mother of Machines: "Permanents entering don't cause abilities of permanents your opponents control to
# trigger" applies to Elesh Norn's own entering (the rulings: "a permanent entering the battlefield at the same time as
# Elesh Norn (still including Elesh Norn) won't cause abilities of permanents an opponent controls to trigger"), and the
# doubling doesn't care who controls the entering permanent ("Elesh Norn's abilities don't look at who controls the
# permanent entering the battlefield").
# Both players have Authority of the Consuls ("Whenever a creature an opponent controls enters, you gain 1 life"). On
# turn 3 Bot1's first Ornithopter, before Elesh Norn, gives Bot2 1 life (the control); Elesh Norn entering and a second
# Ornithopter after it give Bot2 nothing. On turn 4 Bot2's Ornithopter triggers Bot1's Authority twice: Bot1 gains 2.

